   00001| //! Additive edits and the words that place them (issues #1115, #1116, #1133).
   00002| //!
   00003| //! "Add a line X directly after the line Y in F" names no old→new pair, so the
   00004| //! replacement composer in `general_planner` answered it with nothing and the
   00005| //! request went to web search. The anchor line is the text an edit tool can
   00006| //! match exactly, and the replacement is the anchor with the new line beside
   00007| //! it -- so an insertion is an edit after all, and no insert primitive is
   00008| //! needed. Which side of the position cue the anchor sits on is a fact of the
   00009| //! cue's language (`languages.lino`, `adposition`), not of the sentence.
